Hi Jozsef

I seem to have a small problem with the window-handling in
tcp-window-tracking.

I see cases where it thinks ACK from my machine is over the upper bound
and SEQ from the remote host is over the upper bound.

I've seen it mostly on irc connections, in other words, long lived
connections.
I didn't have ip_conntrack_log_invalid set for tcp the first times so
for those cases I only have the output of my ULOG rule for INVALID
packets.
Then I set it to log invalid tcp and since then (set it yesterday) I've
had one occation where it complained and marked packets as invalid.

The first packet it complained about is originating from my machine in
the attached log. X.X.X.X is my machine, it's an normal desktop and
tcp-window-tracking is running on it (end host).

Now I've started a tcpdump to see what really happens when it complains.
Hopefully I'll have something more substantial that this report soon.

--=20
/Martin

